\pard\ulnone\fs22                                      Montecarlo Scarface, version 2.d, by 27-may-2013.\lang1033\kerning0\f0\fs20\par
\par
 \fs22  \lang1040\kerning1\f1\par
  Montecarlo Scarface \kerning0 is an evolution of\fs20  \kerning1 MCockroach 2a\fs22 . \kerning0 I have changed the name.\par
\lang1033\f0\fs20   \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\li142\ri120\lang2057\kerning1\f2\fs24 Montecarlo Scarface is a tool for analysis Monte Carlo.\par
Starting from the position to analyze the program generates hundreds of games to choose the \par
moves in  pseudo random way. The program then displays the results of games resulting from \par
any single move taken into account.\par
The pseudo random way with which the program chooses the moves, is controlled by the user,\par
through the options and parameters of use of the program.\par
\par
\b\fs22 Functioning of the program user interface:\par
\par
\b0 "\b GUI\b0 " means the graphical user interface that is displayed in a window of Windows, when \par
program startup. (The principal window).\par
\par
\pard\li142\ri120\kerning0 To the startup of the program, is displayed on the monitor a GUI, in which are present\par
of the controls that allow to the user to change the parameters and the options of analysis\par
of the tool.\par
In the GUI they are displayed:\par
- the parameters controls of the engine of analysis.\par
\pard\tx708\tx1418\tx2126\tx2836\tx3544\tx4254\tx4962\tx5672\tx6380\tx7090\tx7798\tx8508\tx9216\tx9926   - the "\b Chessboard set position\b0 " button, to plan the position in analysis.\par
\pard\li142\ri120 - the "\b start\b0 " button , to initialize the analysis.\par
- the "\b stop\b0 " button, to stop the analysis.\par
- the "\b View log\b0 " button, to display the log.\par
- the "\b Reset log\b0 " button, to clear the content of the log.\par
\pard   - the "\b Help\b0 " button, to read these instructions.\par
  - Nine "\b progressbar\b0 " for the graphic representation of the results of the analysis, reported\par
\pard\li142\ri120   to the three best movements.\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\li142\ri120\kerning1 To the start the program the parameters of analysis are set with the default values. The user\par
can change these values using parameters controls displayed in the GUI, as change the \par
parameters of a normal engine.\par
\par
\pard\li142\tx708\tx1418\tx2126\tx2836\tx3544\tx4254\tx4962\tx5672\tx6380\tx7090\tx7798\tx8508\tx9216\tx9926\kerning0\ul\b\fs24 To insert the position to analyze:\par
\ulnone\par
\b0\fs22 Click on the "\b Chessboard set position\b0 " button. It will open the "\b Board" \b0 window, where user\par
set the position to analyze.\par
The user can past the Fen or to set the position from chessboard, in the following ways:\par
\par
\b 1 - to set the position from FEN:\par
\b0 To past the string FEN in the "\b FEN\b0 " text box  \b .\b0  Press "\b Load fen\b0 " button\b . \b0 To close the\par
 "\b Board\b0 " window. \b\par
\b0 (With the Chessbase programs  type Fritz, click on edit>copy position and then past the fen).\par
\par
\b 2 - to set the position from the chessboard:\par
\b0 To set the pieces in the chessboard. At the end press on the "\b Load board\b0 " button.\b  (\b0 The modified\f1\fs24\par
\f2\fs22 position is load in the "\b FEN\b0 " textbox  ). Press therefore on the button "\b Load fen\b0 ".\b  \par
\b0 To close the "\b Board\b0 " window.\b\par
\par
3 - to set the position from FEN and therefore to modify the position from the chessboard:\par
\b0 To past the string FEN in the "\b FEN\b0 " textbox. Press on the "\b Load fen\b0 " button .\b  \par
\b0 Set the position in the chessboard, at the end press on the "\b Load board\b0 " button.\b  \b0 Then\par
press still on the "\b Load fen\b0 " button.\b  \b0 To close the "\b Board\b0 " window. \b\par
\pard\tx708\tx1418\tx2126\tx2836\tx3544\tx4254\tx4962\tx5672\tx6380\tx7090\tx7798\tx8508\tx9216\tx9926\par
\pard\li142\tx708\tx1418\tx2126\tx2836\tx3544\tx4254\tx4962\tx5672\tx6380\tx7090\tx7798\tx8508\tx9216\tx9926\ul\b0 Important:\ulnone   \i to the analysis engine is sent always the fen \f1\fs20 displayed\fs22  \f2 in the "FEN"\par
textbox . Then if user set or manually modifies the position  from the chessboard,\par
press needs always both on the button "Load board" and subsequently on the button\par
"Load fen". \par
\par
\ul To set  autostop function:\par
\ulnone If  you wanted to set a maximum duration for the session of analysis,checked the \par
checkbox "\b Auto stop\b0 ", before of choosing the moves.\b\par
\b0 To set the overall number of games for the session of analysis, set the number in "\b n.Games\b0 " control.\par
Reached the number of games set with "\b n.Games\b0 ", the analysis will automatically stop.\par
\par
\pard\par
\pard\li142\tx708\tx1418\tx2126\tx2836\tx3544\tx4254\tx4962\tx5672\tx6380\tx7090\tx7798\tx8508\tx9216\tx9926\b\i0\par
\pard\li142\tx142\tx708\tx1418\tx2126\tx2836\tx3544\tx4254\tx4962\tx5672\tx6380\tx7090\tx7798\tx8508\tx9216\ul\fs24 To save the played games: \par
\ulnone\b0\fs22 Check the checkbox "\b Save pgn"\b0 , before the choice moves.\par
When the user presses the "\b Stop\b0 " button, to stop the analysis, will open the window "\b Save games\b0 ".\par
To press the "\b Save pgn\b0 " button (in the window "Save games") and to save the pgn file in a folder to choice. \par
If you doesn't press the  "\b Save pgn\b0 " button, when is closed the "\b Save games\b0 " window , all the data games\par
will be deleted. The pgn file gotten, can be read by a chess GUI type Fritz, and eventually imported in a\par
opening book.\par
\pard\par
